// spec: a template parameter deduces from an overloaded function's name given for a pointer to function: of the overloads, the one whose type deduces is taken ([temp.deduct.call] 6): `apply(over, 4)` of `template<typename R> R apply(R (*f)(int), int)` with over(int) and over(double) takes over(int), R = int (clang's output)
// pending: "codegen does not support a call to apply whose template arguments could not be deduced yet": an overload set deduces nothing (found by D's deduction battery against clang, 2026-11-10; D)
int over(int x) { return x + 1; }
double over(double x) { return x * 2; }
template<typename R>
R apply(R (*f)(int), int x) { return f(x); }

int main()
{
  std::println(apply(over, 4));
  return 0;
}
